  "anonQuotaReportKeptBody": "The limit of reports without an account is reached. This report is kept on this phone and will be sent as soon as you create an account or sign in.",
  "anonQuotaOpen": "Why a limit?",
  "errorAnonQuotaExhausted": "The limit of reports without an account is reached on this device. Please create an account.",
  "intro1Title": "Welcome to e-Himaya",
  "intro1Body": "e-Himaya finds your position from your phone. In an emergency it sends it with your report straight to the competent Civil Protection operations room, so help reaches you faster and with the right resources.",
  "intro2Title": "Run by the National Civil Protection Office",
  "intro2Body": "This app is provided by the National Civil Protection Office, the public body in charge of rescue, firefighting and disaster response across Tunisia, which answers the 198 emergency line.",
  "intro3Title": "When should I use it?",
  "intro3Body": "Fire, road accident, a person in danger or injured, drowning, collapse, gas leak, flood, or any situation that threatens lives or property and needs Civil Protection.",
  "intro4Title": "How does it work?",
  "intro4Body": "Choose the type of incident, add a photo, video or voice message if you can do so safely, and send. Your report and position reach the operator at once; you can follow it step by step and the operator may call you back. Without internet the report goes by SMS, and calling 198 is always available.",
  "intro5Title": "Where does it work?",
  "intro5Body": "Throughout the Republic of Tunisia, in all 24 governorates; your report is routed automatically to the competent regional directorate. Outside Tunisia, call the local emergency number (112 in most countries).",
  "terms1Title": "1. Purpose",
  "terms1Body": "e-Himaya is a digital platform of the National Civil Protection Office (\"the Office\") for reporting emergencies and following them up. These terms govern the relationship between the Office and the users of the mobile app and the institutions portal.",
  "terms2Title": "2. Our mission",
  "terms2Body": "To protect lives and property, and to rebuild trust between citizens and Civil Protection through direct and open communication. Describing the incident accurately and showing the scene as it is shortens response time and makes the intervention more effective.",
  "terms3Title": "3. Nature and limits of the service",
  "terms3Body": "3.1 The app complements 198 and does not replace it. In immediate danger, call 198 directly.\n3.2 The app gives no medical advice; its safety tips are for general awareness and do not replace the instructions of Civil Protection staff.\n3.3 It depends on factors outside the Office's control: mobile network and internet coverage, location signal, battery and the condition of the phone. The Office aims for the highest availability and fixes faults as fast as possible.",
  "terms4Title": "4. User obligations",
  "terms4Body": "4.1 Use the app in good faith and only for real emergencies; give accurate, up-to-date information, especially your phone number.\n4.2 Keep location turned on and use the latest version of the app.\n4.3 Do not put yourself in danger to film, and follow the instructions of responders.\n4.4 Do not harm, disrupt, bypass the protections of, or reverse-engineer the app.",
  "terms5Title": "5. False alarms and misuse",
  "terms5Body": "Every report sends out rescue teams that other lives may need at the same moment. A deliberate false report or any misuse of the app exposes its author to prosecution under Tunisian law, and may lead to temporary or permanent suspension of the account or of reporting from the device concerned.",
  "terms6Title": "6. Institutions' obligations",
  "terms6Body": "A registered institution provides accurate, up-to-date information on its identity, activity, buildings and managers, and is responsible for it. Filing and updating the evacuation plan and building plans makes the intervention easier and shortens search and rescue inside the building. The account is activated only after the Office approves it.",
  "terms7Title": "7. Volunteers",
  "terms7Body": "Volunteer status is granted only after the Office approves it. Volunteers follow the operations room's instructions and act only within the task assigned to them.",
  "terms8Title": "8. Personal data protection",
  "terms8Body": "8.1 Personal data is processed under Organic Law No. 2004-63 of 27 July 2004 on the protection of personal data, under the supervision of the National Authority for the Protection of Personal Data (INPDP), solely to handle emergencies and to keep you informed about your reports.\n8.2 When you send a report, the Office receives your position, the type of incident, the description and attached media, and your account details if you have an account.\n8.3 Emergency contacts and the text of your SOS message are stored encrypted on your phone only and are never sent to the Office.\n8.4 You can report without an account under a pseudonym; your IP address is not recorded.\n8.5 Only authorised staff can access the data, which is kept as long as needed to handle the case and meet legal obligations. You have the right to access, correct and object to the processing of your data.",
  "terms9Title": "9. Changes to the app and these terms",
  "terms9Body": "The Office may improve the app or change these terms. You are told about each new version and what it contains, and asked to accept again when the terms change.",
  "terms10Title": "10. Applicable law",
  "terms10Body": "These terms are governed by Tunisian law; Tunisian courts have jurisdiction over any dispute.",
